iew Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really a campaign but we noticed few of us had a version of Arms of the Chosen with a mistake in it because the Artefact Ship of one of the players had something like 24 hp.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, that's even better with Blood and Salt Bondage!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From what I've read the main problem of Naval Battle is that (for Solars) it's all about having a huge score and all the Charms are useless because you already have a huge score (you're a Solar) and going beyond is pretty pointless </div> </div> </div>Are they not helpful against exalt foes with big scores? Other than that having multiple enemies, time pressure, and other drains on motes could all help make them more relevant.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T12:32:08-07:00","id":1374614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374578-your-experiences-with-naval-combat?p=1374606#post1374606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow, that's even better with Blood and Salt Bondage!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Are they not helpful against exalt foes with big scores? Other than that having multiple enemies, time pressure, and other drains on motes could all help make them more relevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm really not expert on this topic but I think the Naval Battle Charm experts will soon fly in and explain these in greater details. It's useful to fight another all powerful Solar with thousands of successes as well, but except for that it's apparently pretty redundant<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12314_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12314\" data-vbnamecard=\"12314\">Grod_the_giant</a> How is Salty Dog Method weird ? The only thing I'm not sure to understand is the &quot;fall down fall up&quot; thingy and I suspect it's because my English is not good enough to understand what this means","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T15:40:40-07:00","id":1374642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374578-your-experiences-with-naval-combat?p=1374614#post1374614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12314_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12314\" data-vbnamecard=\"12314\">Grod_the_giant</a> How is Salty Dog Method weird ? The only thing I'm not sure to understand is the &quot;fall down fall up&quot; thingy and I suspect it's because my English is not good enough to understand what this means</div> </div> </div> </div>It's weird in that the forum apparently only ate half my post. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> What I <i>meant </i>to say was that Sail is odd in that it has three main trees. The ones building off Salty Dog Method and Ship-Claiming Stance have the usual mix of cool stuff, while the one branching from Immortal Mariner's Advantage is pretty much entirely &quot;roll better during naval combat&quot;-- but there are enough relevant Charms in the other two trees that you could probably axe the whole thing with no loss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T15:53:16-07:00","id":1374643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374578-your-experiences-with-naval-combat?p=1374642#post1374642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's weird in that the forum apparently only ate half my post. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> What I <i>meant </i>to say was that Sail is odd in that it has three main trees. The ones building off Salty Dog Method and Ship-Claiming Stance have the usual mix of cool stuff, while the one branching from Immortal Mariner's Advantage is pretty much entirely &quot;roll better during naval combat&quot;-- but there are enough relevant Charms in the other two trees that you could probably axe the whole thing with no loss.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thus my &quot;brilliant&quot; idea of playing a game with 3 separate Solar sailors who take three different sections of the charm tree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}